        "content": "**SLO** - a promise about user experience: at least the target share of requests (99 % by default) must succeed *and* start answering within a per-class time (TTFT).\n\n**Error budget** - the share of requests that are allowed to break the promise. *Budget left* shows how much of it the selected time range has not yet used.\n\n**Burn rate** - how fast the budget is being used: 1x is exactly on budget, 6x would empty a budget in one sixth of its period. That is why the pager fires at 6x and a ticket opens at 2.5x.\n\n**Markers** - red = a fault the harness injected (with its name on hover), purple = an experiment run, yellow = a burn-rate alert firing.\n\nNext: **Incident view** to see what broke and where, **Autoscaling experiment** to see how capacity followed the load.",
